==Multi-combat mechanics==
{{map:Multicombat_AGT}}

Although the entire [[Ancient Guthixian Temple]] is considered a [[single-way combat]] zone by the game, the temple is a unique outlier in the fact that some areas are pseudo-[[multicombat area]]s. While in the temple, an icon that depicts a tormented demon's head (shown below) can be seen in the user interface, indicating the number of demons the player can engage at one time. Other players will be unable to attack a demon that is engaged in combat with another player until that player leaves by any means.

<gallery widths="125" heights="125" mode="nolines">
File:Tormented demons multicombat I.png|'''Single-Combat:''' 10 demons—The [[Plinth (Ancient Guthixian Temple)|plinth]] chamber in the south-east contains eight demons in a single-combat area. Two additional single-demon rooms can be found in the north-west of the temple (directly west of the temple entrance).  
File:Tormented demons multicombat II.png|'''Double-Combat:''' 10 demons—The central chamber and the four eastern rooms each contain two demons.  
File:Tormented demons multicombat III.png|'''Triple-Combat:''' 6 demons—Two rooms in the south-west contain three demons each.  
</gallery>Tormented demons are unaggressive and will not attack unless attacked first.
==Fight overview==
{{main|Tormented Demon/Strategies}}

Tormented demons can pray against and attack using every [[combat style]]. They possess the ability to routefind, allowing them to move around objects, and can also stack on top of each other. If they cannot reach the player when attempting to melee, they will instead randomly fire magic and ranged attacks.

Every 150 health lost since their last prayer swap (roughly 25% of their max health), they will change their protection prayer to the last combat style they were damaged with, and will stop attacking for 6 [[tick]]s (3.6s).

They will briefly bind the player in place roughly every 60 ticks (36s; 10 attacks) and disable run ({{Key press|Ctrl}} clicking still allows running), then release two fire bombs: one on the player's position as of the start of the attack, and a second on a random one of the 8 adjacent squares, assuming that it is a walkable tile. The bind will then be released and players have 2 ticks to move off of the target tiles before they explode. The demons always change their combat style after this attack. 

Tormented demons usually have a fire shield that reduces damage done by non-[[demonbane weapons]]/[[demonbane spells|spells]] and non-[[abyssal weapons]] by 20%. They will drop this shield after the player's first attack and after each fire bomb attack; the shield remains down until they are attacked once. Slower weapons will deal significant bonus damage to unshielded tormented demons. They also become defenseless, indicated by the flames on their body disappearing, approximately 30 ticks (18s; 5 attacks) into the fight until after their fire bomb attack, after which the 30 tick timer begins again. Attacking them while defenseless will provide 100% accuracy meaning guaranteed hits.

The [[clickbox]] of a tormented demon will shift whenever their shield animation plays (every few ticks). This can affect clicking away from the demon during a fire bomb. Changing their shift-click to walk through is a good preventative measure for this, as well as tagging tormented demons with their tag style set to hull in order to more accurately see their [[clickbox]].

If the player chooses to attack multiple tormented demons simultaneously, their attack behaviour changes: one will use melee if possible, and the other magic or ranged, and their attacks start out staggered so they can be prayed against. If three or more demons are attacking the player, the third and any more demons will release single bombs at the player.

If demons are forced out of combat due to teleportation or being unable to attack their target, they will restore their health to full.

