==Development history==
Tormented demons were released alongside While Guthix Sleeps on [[26 November]] [[2008]], during the period often referred to as ''RuneScape 2''. The version found in ''Old School'' is very similar, but has several differences both with the original ''RuneScape 2'' version and their modern ''RuneScape 3'' counterparts:

*There are significantly more tormented demons throughout the entirety of the Ancient Guthixian Temple. In ''RuneScape 3'', there are only six demons, all of whom are near the plinth where the Stone of Jas once was, while in ''Old School RuneScape'', there are twenty-six; eight by the plinth, two by the door leading to the inner section of the temple, eight to the western section of the temple (one each to the north-western chambers, and two sets of three to the south-west) and another eight to the eastern dolmens, in four sets of two.
*The tormented demons in ''Old School RuneScape'' are unaggressive, whereas those in ''RuneScape 3'' never become tolerant to the player.
*In ''Old School RuneScape'', tormented demons are considered [[greater demon]]s for the purpose of a slayer assignment. In ''RuneScape 3'', tormented demons were not an assignable Slayer task for a considerable amount of time after release, and later became unlockable through Slayer points or killable as part of a {{RSL|demons (Slayer assignment)|demon cluster task}}.
* Tormented demons in both games attack with all three combat styles, but have somewhat different mechanics:
** When changing attack styles in ''RuneScape 3'', they use an AoE magic attack in their immediate area. This occurs every 16 seconds. In ''Old School RuneScape'', they instead bind the player in place before launching a fire bomb attack at them. This occurs every 36 seconds.
** If using melee but attacked from a distance in ''RuneScape 3'', a tormented demon will immediately change combat styles. In ''Old School RuneScape'', they will only do so if they cannot reach their target, and will randomly switch between magic and ranged to discourage safespotting.
** Tormented demons switch their overhead prayer more frequently in ''RuneScape 3'', doing so after taking 3100 damage (about 15% of their total life points). In ''Old School RuneScape'', they switch after taking 150 damage (25% of their total hitpoints).
** Their fire shield is much stronger in ''RuneScape 3'', reducing all damage by 75% until destroyed by {{RSL|Darklight}} or {{RSL|holy water}}. In ''Old School RuneScape'', the shield reduces non-demonbane damage by 20% and is dropped after being attacked or after using a fire bomb attack for one attack.
*** Additionally, when a tormented demon is attacked while their shield is down, a damage bonus is given based on weapon speed, with slower weapons receiving higher bonuses. This allows for significant bonus damage from non-demonbane weapons, if timed correctly.
*On release in ''RuneScape 2'', tormented demons had four unique drops: {{RSL|dragon claws}} and three pieces of the {{RSL|dragon platebody}}. Later, {{RSL|dragon limbs}} were also added to their drop table. As all of these items were already present in ''Old School RuneScape'' when tormented demons were added, their droptable is significantly different, instead featuring the [[tormented synapse]] and [[burning claws]].
*Tormented demons in ''RuneScape 2'' were originally released with 326 hitpoints and zero offensive or defensive stats. The demons in ''Old School RuneScape'' have 600 hitpoints and have offensive and defensive stats added to give them a distinct weakness:{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://x.com/JagexAsh/status/1749777281675907450|date=23 January 2024|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/27963401|archivedate=7 April 2026|quote=[I was wondering what stats they had before then. Is it possible to find out please?] Attack 255
Strength 166
Defence 300
Magic 255
Ranged 255
Lifepoints 3260 (presumably that's 326 HP)
No defensive bonuses.|name=Tormented demon 2008 stats}}
